  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nMonday and Tuesday will feature seasonably warm temperatures\nacross NE Montana accompanied by isolated to widely scattered\nafternoon and evening thunderstorms while ridging remains\npronounced across the Northern High Plains.\n\nToward the middle of the week a trough will dig into the Pacific\nNorthwest allowing the downstream ridge pattern to amplify as the\nridge axis pushes east. This will eventually send southwest flow\naloft over the region by the second half of the week into the\nupcoming weekend. This pattern will lead to increasing daily\nchances for showers and thunderstorms, with heavy rain potential\nas the monsoonal fetch makes its way into the area. Bottom line:\ncooler and more unsettled weather is likely to emerge by lateweek\ninto the weekend.\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was the guidance of choice for this forecast cycle which\ncaptured expected macro trends well. Consensus has strong support\nfor seasonably warm temperatures to begin with this week before\nconditions become cooler and more unsettled later in the week,\nthough there is divergence on how much QPF will ultimately land\nwhich is expected at later time scales. Confidence should begin to\nimprove as this enters the short term and is picked up by higher\nresolution guidance.",
